/**
 * One transaction: a reversal receipt (total = −original, reverses_receipt_id, reason; no tenders); invoice balance_due restored by the full
receipt amount (cash-limit totals then exclude the reversed receipt's cash); if the original receipt had credit_note tenders, ONE NEW credit note
of kind receipt_reversal (same customer, store_credit_amount = balance_available = their sum, gapless CN number; the original notes are not
topped up). A receipt is reversed at most once (409 receipt_already_reversed); a reversal cannot be reversed (409 receipt_is_reversal);
cancelled bill → 409 invoice_cancelled. The DB raises the owner alert receipt_reversal ("Payment reversed") for the new note.
Requires sales.receipt.reverse (owner, manager). Idempotency-Key required. Audited (sales.receipt.reverse).

 * @summary Reverse a wrong payment receipt (0.9.2): a negative receipt, the balance due restored, store credit given back as a new credit note
 */
